@startuml proxy-toggle-flow
!include _standard-style.puml
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false

title px — toggles your shell's proxy, never stops proxydetox

actor User
participant "px\n(<U+007E>/proxy.sh)" as PX
participant "<U+007E>/.bash_profile\nhttp_proxy= line" as BP
participant "launchd\nproxydetox :3128" as LD
participant "health\ncoordinator" as HC
participant "status line\n(tmux)" as SL

User -> PX: px
alt shell has http_proxy set → OFF
  PX -> BP: comment out http_proxy= (intent: off)
  PX -> PX: unset proxy vars in this shell
  note right of LD
    proxydetox stays loaded: agent sessions
    are pinned to :3128, and it goes DIRECT
    off the corporate network by itself
  end note
else not set → ON
  PX -> LD: launchctl load (if not running)
  opt :3128 does not answer
    PX -> LD: unload + load (stale socket after sleep)
  end
  PX -> BP: uncomment http_proxy= (intent: on)
  PX -> PX: source <U+007E>/.bash_profile
end
PX -> HC: POST /health/refresh (re-probe now)
PX -> SL: delete status-line caches
HC -> HC: proxy_enabled_by_user = intent
SL -> HC: next render (≤ 5 s)
SL --> User: P:ON (working + intent on)\nP:AUTO (working + intent off)\nP:OFF (down / no tunnel, either way)
@enduml
